title: Genres in one place
intro: Match-3, Falling Blocks, Strategy and Tactics are now modules: each genre's components, systems, drawing, templates and Entity menu items live together, and Griff's core names none of them.
project: Empty | Module Garden

chapter: A genre is a module | Match-3, from one folder
say: A match board still comes from the Entity menu, but the menu item, the board, the system that runs it and the Match-3 template now all live in the Match-3 module.
create: Match Board
explain: component:MatchBoard | From the Match-3 module | Griff's core doesn't know this component by name. It reaches it through extension points, the same ones a script can use.
deselect
create: Text
rename: Score
set: Transform.Position = 0, 4.5, 0
add: Counter
set: Counter.Track = *
set: Counter.Output = Score
set: Counter.Format = Score: {0}
explain: field:Counter.Output | Counting an output | A counter used to look for a match board itself. Now the board names its outputs, so any component, a script's too, can feed a counter.
write: Scripts/AutoSwap.cs | genre-modules/AutoSwap.cs
code: Assets/Scripts/AutoSwap.cs | AutoSwap.cs
say: This script plays the board by itself. It names the Match Board without any using line: scripts get every module's types, just as they get Griff's.
hidecode
deselect
create: Empty
rename: Bot
add: AutoSwap
play
wait: 4
explain: game | Swaps, and the score counting | The board swaps, clears and refills, and the counter shows its score.
stop

chapter: Joining in | A script that steers grid movement
say: Grid movement used to check for tactics units by name. Now anything that steers a grid mover is a grid driver: chasers, patrols, pushed crates, tactics units, and scripts.
write: Scripts/Wanderer.cs | genre-modules/Wanderer.cs
code: Assets/Scripts/Wanderer.cs | Wanderer.cs
say: Wanderer is a grid driver. Each time its mover is between steps, it says which way to step next, so it walks a square by itself.
hidecode
select: Board
menu: Entity > Delete
deselect
create: Grid Player
set: Transform.Position = -7, 2, 0
add: Wanderer
play
wait: 1
hold: Up 1
explain: game | Walking its own square | The arrow keys don't move it now. It walks its square, one cell at a time, the way Griff's own enemies and units steer.
wait: 2
stop
say: Strategy and Tactics are modules too, with their own systems, drawing and network commands, and the next genres move the same way.
